# Notice of award and conformance fixture

::: abstract
This document exercises every element in the register exactly as a real administrative notice would, so that closing the vocabulary is tested against use rather than against intent. It is simultaneously the test fixture, the theme validation target, and the golden output.
:::

::: contents
- {{reference target=sec-award}}The award{{/}}
- {{reference target=sec-money}}Amounts{{/}}
- {{reference target=sec-appeal}}Appeal{{/}}
:::

::: section id=sec-award
## The award

The authority has awarded the contract described in {{reference target=sec-money}}Amounts{{/}} to the successful tenderer, with effect from {{date precision=day value=2026-09-01}}. The decision is **final** and, unless *suspended* on appeal, takes effect automatically{{note-ref target=n-effect}}. The reference of record is `9ФΩГ4691Ω2-ΛΛΧ`, published at [the national transparency register](https://diavgeia.gov.gr/decision/view/example).

Issuing authority
: Public Employment Service{{line-break}}Regional Directorate of Epirus
Decision type
: Act of financial content
Protocol number
: 01/07/5702 - 2026

1. The tender was published and the period for expressions of interest has closed.
2. The evaluation committee assessed all admissible tenders against the published criteria.
3. The award follows the committee recommendation without modification.

::: admonition kind=important
Standstill applies. No contract may be signed before {{date precision=day value=2026-09-11}}.
:::

> Contracting authorities shall as soon as possible inform each candidate and tenderer of decisions reached concerning the award of a contract.
> {{source v="Directive 2014/24/EU, Article 55"}}
:::

::: section id=sec-money
## Amounts

All amounts are exact. Currency is carried as an integer significand and a scale, never as a floating point number, so a total is reproducible byte for byte on every client.

Significands are bounded by the encoding, not by the format\: an integer in the range -{{power base=2 exponent=63}} to {{power base=2 exponent=63}}-1 inclusive. Exponentiation is a semantic element rather than a superscript, because a superscript is appearance and this document carries none. It projects to `2^63`, which is the notation the plain text already uses.

